{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-68717",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "To raise the fraction to the power of $3$, we must raise both the numerator and the denominator to the power of $3:$\n\n$$\n{(\\frac{1}{4})}^{3}=\\frac{{1}^{3}}{{4}^{3}}\n$$\n\nNow, using, ${1}^{3}=1$ and ${4}^{3}=64,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{{1}^{3}}{{4}^{3}}=\\frac{1}{64}.\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
